Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [licensing gap, not riscv64-specific, but we distribute the wheel so compliance is ours]

Upstream declares no license/license-files, so scikit-build-core embeds no
LICENSE in the built wheel (confirmed on the published x86_64 wheel). The
build also statically links FFTW (GPL-2.0-or-later, fetched from source by
CMake) into libfinufft.so, so its licence text needs to ship too; a
CIBW_BEFORE_BUILD step stages it as LICENSE.fftw for the license-files glob
to pick up.

diff --git a/python/finufft/pyproject.toml b/python/finufft/pyproject.toml
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/python/finufft/pyproject.toml
+++ b/python/finufft/pyproject.toml
@@ -22,6 +22,8 @@ authors = [
     {name = "Alex Barnett"}]
 maintainers = [{name = "Alex Barnett", email = "abarnett@flatironinstitute.org"}]
 description = "Python interface to FINUFFT"
+license = "Apache-2.0"
+license-files = ["LICENSE*"]
 classifiers = [
     "License :: OSI Approved :: Apache Software License",
     "Programming Language :: Python :: 3",
